# Force a consistent line ending on checkout regardless of the checking-out
# machine's own git config. Without this, a text file committed with LF
# (every source file here always has been) checks out as CRLF on a machine
# with `core.autocrlf=true` -- GitHub's `windows-latest` runner's Git for
# Windows defaults to exactly that. That silently broke vix-tutor's
# exact-match lesson-progress checks the first time real Windows CI actually
# ran them (T547): a test's `.replace("DELETE THIS ENTIRE LINE\n", "")`
# against a CRLF-corrupted buffer never matched, since the pattern's `\n`
# no longer immediately followed the text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuine binaries: never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.gif -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.ico -text
*.woff -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf -text
*.sqlite -text

# Already committed with CRLF (the WiX toolset's own convention for its
# installer config) -- leave it alone rather than force LF and disagree
# with what's already in the repository.
wix/main.wxs -text
